<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nuremberg</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nuremberg is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franconia">Franconia</a>, in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, which became one of the most important <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/free-imperial-city">free imperial cities</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-empire">Holy Roman Empire</a>. Along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankfurt">Frankfurt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/augsburg">Augsburg</a> it grew wealthy as a commercial centre exploiting the empire's central European transit position. It was also a centre of crafts, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/printing-press">printing</a> and humanist learning.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nuremberg.jpg" alt="Nuremberg" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DALIBRI · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:N%C3%BCrnberger_Burg_im_Herbst_2013.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
